                              "disease_code":  "HAEMORRHOIDS",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Haemorrhoids cause bright red blood on the toilet paper or in the pan, typically without change in bowel habit or weight loss. Colonoscopy is required to exclude CRC in patients over 40."
                          },
                          {
                              "disease_code":  "INFLAMMATORY_BOWEL_DISEASE",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "IBD causes rectal bleeding with mucus, abdominal cramping, and systemic inflammation markers. It tends to present in younger patients; CRC risk increases with long-standing IBD."
                          },
                          {
                              "disease_code":  "DIVERTICULAR_DISEASE",
                              "distinguishing_feature":  "Diverticular bleeding is typically painless and large-volume. CRC should be excluded in any patient with diverticular-pattern bleeding by colonoscopy."
